From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasmine <jasmine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0135: gate j0133/j0134 on client-layer swaps; long
 own-frame waits

The j0134 kernel regressed the whole UI.  backboardd's own composited frames
(pid 57, surfaces it created) are swaps with no client layer.  netlog-swap134
shows swap 766 (layer 0, surface 2, pid 57) dropped by j0134's ticket-not-ready
path, then j0133's recovery retires 766 as abandoned; 768 and 770 repeat it, a
200 ms present-scope timeout drops swap 782 ("dropped (1)"), and the queue falls
back (reason 2), so the display is synchronous for the rest of boot.
netlog-swap134b (the same kernel minus the gpuSeqno skip) shows the same once
Maps is exec'd: own frames 428/434/437/440/441/614/... hit the 100 ms ticket
probe, j0133 abandons them, and QUEUE FALLBACK reason 2 follows.  Maps' heavy
jobs are ahead of backboardd's on the single GPU ring (one ring, no priority or
preemption).

Record at SwapEnd/swap() whether a swap contains a layer created by another
process (clientLayer(): surface creatorPID != the SwapEnd caller's pid), in the
queue token and in a per-id swap record for synchronous mode; the highest client
id is kept separately so a reused ring slot cannot hide it from the sync watchdog.
Execute every new j0133/j0134 recovery only when that flag says the swap (or, for
a wait, one of its newer begun/ended swaps) has a client layer:

- j0133 abandonShown/abandon retirement only if one of the newer swaps has a
  client layer, and then only those client-layer newer swaps are retired;
- j0134 ticket-not-ready handling only for a client-layer swap;
- j0134 present-scope drop and queue survival only for a client-layer swap;
- j0134 sync-mode watchdog and noteShown completion only when the waited swap or
  a newer begun/ended swap has a client layer.

Own-only swaps get longer bounds so Maps' GPU work does not drop them:

- ticket/gpuSeqno validation now waits up to SWEET_FB_OWN_TICKET_MS (1000 ms,
  the same bound as queuePresent's tracked-ticket admission) instead of the
  100 ms display probe.  The probe is retried; a cancelled ticket still takes
  the j0132 path at once.  Only the 1000 ms expiry runs j0132's
  rejectFrame(16)/drop.
- the own-only present-scope timeout is SWEET_FB_OWN_SCOPE_MS (1500 ms):
  queuePresent holds fPresentBusy for up to 1000 ms (ticket) + 100 ms (cancel
  quiesce) + 150 ms (waitLatch), so the old 200 ms bound fired inside that
  window.  After 1500 ms j0132's rejectFrame(1)/queueFallback(1)/drop still runs.
  The gpuSeqno-only wait (tickets disabled) uses the same 1000 ms budget.
- client-layer swaps are unchanged: 100 ms ticket/seqno probe, 200 ms scope,
  j0134 drop/complete.

The client-layer ticket bypass stays (that wait cannot be satisfied for another
process's surface).  The sweetfb_abandon and sweetfb_clientlayer kill switches
are unchanged; clientLayer() itself no longer depends on the j0134 switch, so
sweetfb_clientlayer=0 still restores j0133 and the abandon recovery also works
with it off.  No build or boot has been done for this patch.
